														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3565974">
									

<p>I'll be honest, I actually have no idea how they'd go about confirming kills. But to clarify, the 174 -A's they specified as being confirmed kills were all actually recovered and buried after the war. They exhumed a few of the bodies from their graves to see if any of them were 3237, and kept going when they found the anomalous temperature and lack of decomposition.</p>
<p>The 63 they recovered from Kollaa were also killed by Häyhä, but may not count toward his confirmed kills. I don't know if you need to find the body for it to count. And in retrospect, 63 seems like a lot of bodies to miss for 60 years. Maybe me from three years ago should've made that number smaller&#8230;</p>
<p>Oh well. I used the number of bodies to pick the SCP number. Can't change it now.</p>

